{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++11 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nWhile creating high loaded systems one should pay a special attention to caching. This problem will be about one of the most popular caching algorithms called LRU (Least Recently Used).Suppose the cache may store no more than k objects. At the beginning of the workflow the cache is empty. When some object is queried we check if it is present in the cache and move it here if it's not. If there are more than k objects in the cache after this, the least recently used one should be removed. In other words, we remove the object that has the smallest time of the last query.Consider there are n videos being stored on the server, all of the same size. Cache can store no more than k videos and caching algorithm described above is applied. We know that any time a user enters the server he pick the video i with probability pi. The choice of the video is independent to any events before.The goal of this problem is to count for each of the videos the probability it will be present in the cache after 10100 queries.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++11 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef long double ld;\n\nconst ld eps = 1e-6;\nconst int INF = 1e9;\nconst int MAXN = 21;\nconst int MAXMASK = 1 << MAXN;\n\ninline bool eq(ld a, ld b) { return fabs(a - b) < eps; }\n\nint n, N, k, mmask;\nll cnk[MAXN][MAXN];\nld p[MAXN];\nld pSum[MAXMASK];\nint trueId[MAXN], mass[MAXN];\nld ans[MAXN];\nld coeff[MAXN];\n\nvoid printAns() {\n    cout.precision(20);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        cout << ans[i];\n        cout << (i == N - 1 ? '\\n' : ' ');\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    N = n;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) cin >> p[i];\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        if (eq(p[i], 1.0)) {\n            ans[i] = 1.0;\n            printAns();\n            return 0;\n        }\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) trueId[i] = i;\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        if (eq(p[i], 0.0)) {\n            for (int j = i; j < n - 1; ++j) {\n                p[j] = p[j + 1];\n                trueId[j] = trueId[j + 1];\n            }\n            --n;\n            --i;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (n <= k) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) ans[trueId[i]] = 1.0;\n        printAns();\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    cnk[0][0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i < MAXN; ++i) {\n        cnk[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 1; j < MAXN; ++j)\n            cnk[i][j] = cnk[i - 1][j - 1] + cnk[i - 1][j];\n    }\n\n    for (int j = k - 1; j >= 1; --j) {\n        coeff[j] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= k - 1 - j; ++i)\n            coeff[j] -= cnk[n - j - 1][i];\n    }\n\n    mmask = 1 << n;\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < mmask; ++mask) {\n        pSum[mask] = 0;\n        mass[mask] = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n            if (mask & (1 << i)) {\n                pSum[mask] += p[i];\n                mass[mask]++;\n            }\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        ld curAns = 0.0;\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < mmask; ++mask) {\n            int j = mass[mask];\n            if (j >= 1 && j <= k - 1 && !(mask & (1 << i))) {\n                assert(!eq(pSum[mask], 1.0));\n                curAns += coeff[j] * (pSum[mask] / (1.0 - pSum[mask]));\n            }\n        }\n        curAns += 1.0;\n        curAns *= p[i];\n        ans[trueId[i]] = curAns;\n    }\n\n    printAns();\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ntypedef long long ll;\ntypedef long double ld;\n\nconst ld eps = 1e-12;\nconst int INF = 1e9;\nconst int MAXN = 21;\nconst int MAXMASK = 1 << MAXN;\n\ninline bool eq(ld a, ld b) { return fabs(a - b) < eps; }\n\nint n, N, k, mmask;\nld p[MAXN];\nld pSum[MAXMASK];\nint trueId[MAXN];\nld ans[MAXN];\nld coeff[MAXN];\n\nvoid printAns() {\n    cout.precision(15);\n    cout.setf(ios::fixed);\n    for (int i = 0; i < N; ++i) {\n        cout << ans[i];\n        cout << (i == N - 1 ? '\\n' : ' ');\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> n >> k;\n    N = n;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) cin >> p[i];\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) trueId[i] = i;\n\n    // Remove videos with probability 0\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        if (eq(p[i], 0.0)) {\n            for (int j = i; j < n - 1; ++j) {\n                p[j] = p[j + 1];\n                trueId[j] = trueId[j + 1];\n            }\n            --n;\n            --i;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (n <= k) {\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) ans[trueId[i]] = 1.0;\n        printAns();\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    mmask = 1 << n;\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < mmask; ++mask) {\n        pSum[mask] = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i)\n            if (mask & (1 << i)) {\n                pSum[mask] += p[i];\n            }\n    }\n\n    // Calculate coefficients using inclusion-exclusion\n    for (int mask = 0; mask 